+profile (assumed): herdr-graph is a local Rust CLI plus daemon, a Herdr plugin that one operator runs on their own machine to keep a Git-backed graph of coding-agent seats (teamspace = workspace, seat = tab, clone = pane). There is no network exposure and no external user; state is local records committed to Git, so most mistakes are recoverable from history or by re-running a command. The feature under review adds read-only inspection views, so its core purpose is reporting state accurately: a wrong or misleading status is the failure that matters, while latency, resilience and cost findings carry little weight here. Hooks and skills are installed into the operator's own Claude and Codex configs by `setup`, and Codex trusts a new or changed hook only after an interactive review.
