+## Rejected (with reason)
+- [FYI] §2.3 "Where the hook gets the native session id", Claude bullet (`p=$(cat); printf '%s' "$p" | <bin> seat --hook-prompt --stdin-payload; …`); Unchanged behavior "The hook still never fails or blocks its session"; hg-blw.12 acceptance "stdin read is bounded … a held-open stdin still prints and exits within the budget" — The new Claude hook command runs an unbounded `$(cat)` before the prompt print, reversing today's print-first order; the binary-side bound hg-blw.12 requires never applies to the installed Claude command. Mechanism is real (setup_claude.rs:170-172 today prints first and only `session-report` reads stdin; spec line 259 puts `cat` first). Majority (reproduce + refute, 2–1): the bounded-read/held-open criterion lives only in bead hg-blw.12, not the spec; the spec's own promise (line 572) is about exit codes and the cap, not stdin; and the hook already depends on stdin reaching EOF today because `session-report` does an unbounded `read_to_string` (src/cli/session.rs:49-50), so the change moves the EOF wait rather than adding exposure; the finding itself concedes Claude Code normally closes hook stdin and that the held-open case is "not established". Ground-seat dissent (CONFIRM, Should-fix) cites the same lines and the bead text; the majority's evidence addresses it (bead-level criterion, pre-existing EOF dependence), so the default stands. Residual worth a bead wording touch, not a spec fix: hg-blw.12's "held-open stdin still prints within the budget" criterion cannot be met by the emitted Claude command as written, so either the bead should scope that criterion to the Codex command and direct binary calls, or the Claude command should bound the shell read (`timeout`/`head -c`) or let the binary read stdin once and forward the payload.
+- [FYI] §2.3 record JSON and "Such a hook writes `native_session_id: null`"; §2.2 "`message` is set only for `error`"; §2.1 typed-field rule; hg-blw.12 acceptance ("stdin_payload false", "hook predates --stdin-payload; rerun setup", doctor flag) — hg-blw.12's outdated-hook state requires a `stdin_payload` record field and a JSON home for a "rerun setup" notice the spec does not define. Reject 3–0: grep of the spec finds no `stdin_payload`, "predates" or "rerun"; the spec's own handling is consistent (line 260 older hook writes null id until setup rewrites; line 272 null id → `unknown`; `loaded_session: null` is the typed field; line 261 renders "session not identified" and calls the Codex null case "the honest answer"); the spec never requires telling an outdated Claude hook from a Codex payload without `session_id`. All three seats treat it as a bead-versus-spec divergence outside the spec. Note for the fixer: the premise that the bead text names fields and a notice the spec's shape and `message` rule do not permit is undisputed by the seats, so hg-blw.12's acceptance should be aligned with the spec (drop `stdin_payload`/the notice, or add them to §2.3/§2.2 and hg-blw.1's reserved shape) even though this is not confirmed as a spec gap.
