+## Escalations (need human)
+- §2.3 Codex bullet; Status table `current`/`unknown` rows ("the record's `native_session_id` equals/differs from the occupant's"); LoadedInstructions Owns; hg-blw.12 acceptance "a positive Codex test with a payload session_id records it (source hook-codex)" — The Codex `current`/`stale` path assumes the Codex SessionStart payload `session_id` is byte-equal to the occupant's `native_session_id`, which graph takes from Herdr `agent_session` or `resume <id>` argv (src/model/harness.rs:99-102, CODEX has no hook-reported source; src/observe/sessions.rs:38-45 reduces an `AgentSession::Path` to its file stem); the spec neither states nor tests this equality, and no test drives a Codex clone to `current`, so Codex seats could read `unknown` permanently even with a payload id. Route: UNVERIFIED external (ground seat; reproduce and refute seats REJECT as "honest `unknown`, spec already best-effort for Codex"). Left open by: ground seat's https://herdr.dev/docs/integrations/ ("The Codex hook reports session identity through the same local socket API") which suggests but does not show the two ids are the same value and format; reproduce seat's https://herdr.dev/docs/session-state/ ("Codex | `codex resume <id>`") and https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/hooks (`session_id`: "Current Codex session id", no format given). The only repo evidence of a path-kind Codex `agent_session` is a synthetic fixture (src/herdr/tests.rs:205). Relevant cross-panel fact: two seats on the Codex re-trust panel fetched the same official hooks page and it does list `session_id` in SessionStart stdin, so the spec's "no evidence Codex sends it today" premise is likely wrong and the Codex path is likelier to be exercised than the spec assumes. Cheapest human check: start Codex in a Herdr pane with a logging SessionStart hook, compare the logged `session_id` with the pane's `agent_session` and the committed occupant's `native_session_id`, before and after /clear. If they differ, the spec needs a normalisation rule (or a Herdr-side binding) and hg-blw.12's Codex acceptance should assert `current` against an observer-captured occupant, not just that the id was recorded; if they match, add that assertion and drop the "no evidence" sentence.
